{"text": "One site might be a fluke. So go north-east, to the flat wet country of Lower Saxony in northern Germany. More than 550 wooden paths are known there, laid across bogs and soaked ground, from the Stone Age into modern times. And beside one of those paths, diggers found a thing that had no business being there. Hold on to that — we'll come back for it. Some of the oldest paths sit near a lake called the Deemer. One of them, a path labeled P-R thirty-one, crossed a bog called the Kahm-puh-mohr. It's around six and a half thousand years old — the studies differ on the exact years, so hold that number loosely. It ran up to four and a half metres wide. And it had layers: thin birch trunks at the bottom, three rows of pine logs as a base, a surface of pine logs up to 20 centimetres thick, pinned along the edges with birch pegs. Base, bed, surface. That is road engineering — done with stone axes. The chop marks are still on the ends of the logs. And thirty metres to one side, there runs a second path, laid roughly seventeen hundred years later. Same bog, same problem, same answer.", "alignment": {"characters": ["O", "n", "e", " ", "s", "i", "t", "e", " ", "m", "i", "g", "h", "t", " ", "b", "e", " ", "a", " ", "f", "l", "u", "k", "e", ".", " ", "S", "o", " ", "g", "o", " ", "n", "o", "r", "t", "h", "-", "e", "a", "s", "t", ",", " ", "t", "o", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "f", "l", "a", "t", " ", "w", "e", "t", " ", "c", "o", "u", "n", "t", "r", "y", " ", "o", "f", " ", "L", "o", "w", "e", "r", " ", "S", "a", "x", "o", "n", "y", " ", "i", "n", " ", "n", "o", "r", "t", "h", "e", "r", "n", " ", "G", "e", "r", "m", "a", "n", "y", ".", " ", "M", "o", "r", "e", " ", "t", "h", "a", "n", " ", "5", "5", "0", " ", "w", "o", "o", "d", "e", "n", " ", "p", "a", "t", "h", "s", " ", "a", "r", "e", " ", "k", "n", "o", "w", "n", " ", "t", "h", "e", "r", "e", ",", " ", "l", "a", "i", "d", " ", "a", "c", "r", "o", "s", "s", " ", "b", "o", "g", "s", " ", "a", "n", "d", " ", "s", "o", "a",